# =========================================================================
# Maison - EXAMPLE environment file
#
# Copy this file to ".env" and put the real values in the copy.
# ".env" is listed in .gitignore, so it can never be committed.
# This file (.env.example) must only ever contain placeholders.
# =========================================================================

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FRONT END - these two DO get shipped to the browser, and that is fine.
#
# Anything starting with REACT_APP_ is baked into the public JavaScript
# bundle that every visitor downloads. Only ever put PUBLIC values here.
#
# The Supabase "anon" key is public by design. It is only safe because Row
# Level Security is switched on for every table and bucket - see
# supabase/migrations/. NEVER put the service_role key here.
#
# Where to find these: Supabase dashboard > Project Settings > API
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
REACT_APP_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
REACT_APP_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-supabase-anon-public-key

# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER ONLY - do NOT put these in a REACT_APP_ or VITE_ variable, and do
# not put them in this repo at all. They are set as Edge Function secrets:
#
#   supabase secrets set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-real-anthropic-key
#   supabase secrets set ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://your-app.vercel.app
#
# ...or in the dashboard: Supabase > Edge Functions > Secrets.
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY  Your Anthropic API key. Server side only. It is read
#                    by the Edge Functions and never sent to the browser.
#
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS   Comma separated list of the websites allowed to call
#                    the Edge Functions. Anything else is refused.
#
#                    Every Vercel preview deploy gets its own address, so
#                    ONE entry may contain a single "*" to cover them all.
#                    Example value (all on ONE line, no spaces after the
#                    commas):
#
#                      https://your-app.vercel.app,
#                      https://your-project-*-your-account.vercel.app,
#                      http://localhost:3000
#
#                    Wildcard rules: https only; there must be real text
#                    on BOTH sides of the "*"; and what the "*" matches
#                    can never contain a dot. So a bare "*", "https://*"
#                    and "https://*.vercel.app" are all refused. Only the
#                    first wildcard entry is used.
#
#                    If this is empty, the functions refuse everything on
#                    purpose - that is the safe default, not a bug.
#
# SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_ANON_KEY are injected automatically by Supabase
# when an Edge Function runs, so you never set those two yourself.
# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
